{"artifact_id":"art_e3589efac4f491c198c3a009","artifact_refs":["art_e3589efac4f491c198c3a009"],"attempt_no":1,"canonical_url":"https://jina.ai/reader/","chunker_id":"","chunker_version":"","claim_spec_id":"claim-jina-rate-limit-evidence","content_type":"text/plain","evidence_id":"evidence-source-10","locator":{"section":"Rate Limit; FAQ: What's the rate limit?","type":"section"},"parser_id":"","parser_version":"","quality":{"authority":"official_or_original","directness":"direct","freshness":"verified_2026-08-26","independence":"source_specific","locator_quality":"exact_excerpt","methodological_fit":"fit"},"retrieved_at":"2026-08-26T00:00:00Z","run_id":"run-transient-a1-20260826","schema_version":"1","snapshot_id":"snap_fc5f317e58b69e9b213daf1406e7b4240a67e351987167da6385cfe1561b855c","source_id":"source-a1-jina-reader","stance":"support","step_id":"step-source-10","task_id":"task-source-10","text":"Rate limits are tracked in three ways: **RPM** (requests per minute), and **TPM** (tokens per minute). Limits are enforced per IP/API key and will be triggered when either the RPM or TPM threshold is reached first. When you provide an API key in the request header, we track rate limits by key rather than IP address."}
